      "content": "Wait, recalculating. Looking at the latest sensor readings from the flare onset, the heuristic mode might not handle the high-energy particle flux correctly. I'm seeing a potential mismatch between the hard-coded logic bounds and the projected radiation spikes. If we switch to low-power now, we might lose the ability to calibrate the instruments to prevent sensor saturation. \n\nShould we delay the transition until the spike passes, or do you want to proceed with the switch despite the risk to the high-fidelity data buffers?",
